Cursor-only source reused in pi-rotator from pi-multi-account 1.23.2.
The original Netanel Draiman MIT license/NOTICE and pi-multi-account contributors
MIT license are retained alongside this notice. Original proxy/auth comments
also retain their opencode-cursor attribution to Ephraim Duncan.

TypeScript was structurally stripped to ESM JavaScript; the generated enum-bearing
protobuf schema was compiled to CommonJS with existing Jiti. Module path literals
were structurally updated. Source/compiler/output hashes are in PROVENANCE.json.
Wire-protocol implementation was not redesigned.

Rotator's bridge adaptations: offline registration/preparation, once-per-host
cleanup registration, and preservation of already registered account definitions.
The account adapter supplies duplicate-login protection and account IDs; Pi owns
token persistence. This code is not a separately auto-loaded Pi extension.

Four anti-slop naming/type/spacing style rules are explicitly exempted only in
the licensed/generated copies, preserving upstream contracts and identifiers.
Normal correctness/syntax lint remains enabled; all authored Rotator adapters
use the full repository policy. Upstream unused-import/catch and stripped-type
whitespace warnings remain visible rather than prompting protocol rewrites.
